{"user": "how do i identify what moves would be left for white?", "user_ts": "2026-08-04T13:37:20.135162+00:00", "assistant": "To find White\u2019s replies, do this after you \u201ctry\u201d a Black move:\n\n1. **Place your Black disc and flip the captured Whites.**\n2. Now look at each empty square.\n3. For White to play there, that empty square must touch a **Black disc**, and continuing in that same line there must be a **White disc** to \u201cclose\u201d the sandwich.\n\nSo for White, you\u2019re looking for patterns like:\n\n**empty square \u2192 Black(s) \u2192 White**\n\nin any of the 8 directions.\n\nIf White has **no legal moves**, White must **pass**, and Black plays again.", "assistant_started_ts": "2026-08-04T13:37:32.398866+00:00", "assistant_ts": "2026-08-04T13:37:35.023230+00:00", "annotation_user": {"final": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"], "consensus": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"], "votes": {"Knowledge Deficit Question": 3}, "confidence": {"Knowledge Deficit Question": 1.0}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"], "llama": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"], "sonnet": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "needs_review": false, "arbiter_used": false}, "annotation_assistant": {"final": ["Direct Instruction"], "consensus": ["Direct Instruction"], "votes": {"Direct Instruction": 3, "Prompt": 1}, "confidence": {"Direct Instruction": 1.0, "Prompt": 0.3333333333333333}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["Direct Instruction"], "llama": ["Direct Instruction", "Prompt"], "sonnet": ["Direct Instruction"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "needs_review": false, "arbiter_used": false}, "annotation_assistant_fine": {"final": ["General Principle"], "consensus": ["General Principle"], "votes": {"General Principle": 3, "Hint": 1, "Board Report": 1}, "confidence": {"General Principle": 1.0, "Hint": 0.3333333333333333, "Board Report": 0.3333333333333333}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["General Principle", "Hint